The '''Karamja Dungeon''' is located underneath the [[Karamja Volcano]], and the '''Crandor Dungeon''' is located underneath [[Crandor]]. Both dungeons are connected to each other. In order for a player to gain full access to the Crandor dungeon, they must have completed or be about to engage in the final fight in the quest [[Dragon Slayer I]]. No part of the dungeons are [[multicombat]] zones.

==Transportation==
The Karamja entrance to the dungeon can be accessed by travelling to [[Musa Point]] or [[Brimhaven]] via ship, then walking west or east, respectively, to the [[Karamja Volcano]]. The eastern lip of the volcano has rocks that can be climbed down.

The dungeon can also be accessed by using the [[Minigame Teleport]] to [[TzHaar Fight Pit]], travelling east through [[Mor Ul Rek]], then exiting via the cave to the north.

The Crandor side of the dungeon must first be unlocked during [[Dragon Slayer I]]. After that, it can be accessed by passing the hidden door at the north end of the Karamja side of the dungeon. The door becomes usable after crash-landing on Crandor.

==Notable features==
[[File:Crandor_and_Karamja_Dungeon_map.png|thumb|right|275px|A labelled map of the dungeon.]]
*There is a [[Wall (Crandor and Karamja Dungeon)|wall]] in the Crandor Dungeon, and when pushed, it will take the player to Karamja Dungeon, but only if the player has sailed to [[Crandor]] for [[Dragon Slayer I]]. That is how both dungeons are connected.
*A dragon named [[Elvarg]] lives under Crandor. In order to complete Dragon Slayer I, the player must slay her. Elvarg can only be defeated once, during the quest.
*There is an entrance to the city of [[Mor Ul Rek]], which only members have access to. You go into the Karamja Dungeon main entrance and go into the big opening near the [[rope]].
*There are [[skeleton]]s, [[giant bat]]s, [[deadly red spider]]s, and [[lesser demon]]s under the volcano. So it is recommended that a player brings food if they are intending to enter.
*There are 4 [[gold]] rocks in the [[Karamja Volcano mine]], but they are guarded by aggressive level 22 skeletons.
*There are also [[red spiders' eggs]] respawns.
*It is also quite close to the Karamja docks making the docks a useful place to fish for food to go in with.
*An unreachable tunnel filled with lava stretching to the east is visible to the south-east of the dungeon, featuring three unattackable [[fire giant]]s. These fire giants are intended to reference [[Branda the Fire Queen]]'s lair being nearby.

